{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"Verifier run 2 passed all 43 workloads and confirmed the native dispatcher is safe. It also exposed sharp tile boundaries the coarse buckets missed—for example, `M=72` reaches `0.104 ms` while nearby choices flatten at `0.165 ms`, and the current `M≈2K` choice regresses. I’m now benchmarking a union of the strongest native kernels at every exact workload shape, with `torch.mm` as a conservative candidate, before spending the next verifier run."}}
