{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"agent_message","text":"Run 3 remains fully correct and improves many reference heuristic cliffs, but several local winners were not stable under the harness. I’m restoring the verifier-proven small-shape IDs and testing the alternative hipBLASLt solution dispatcher on representative shapes; this is the last major route that could lower the recurring `~0.164 ms` native floor before I use the final two runs for a conservative comparison and confirmation."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport torch,triton,aiter,time\nB=torch.randn((6144,4096),device='cuda',dtype=torch.float16); BT=B.T\naiter.hipb_create_extension(); tops={}; t0=time.time()\nfor m in [64,128,224,256,972,2053,2379,8192]:\n A=torch.randn((m,4096),device='cuda',dtype=torch.float16)\n sols=torch.ops.aiter.hipb_findallsols(A,BT)\n vals=[]\n for idx in sols:\n  fn=lambda idx=idx:torch.ops.aiter.hipb_mm(A,BT,idx)\n  try: vals.append((triton.testing.do_bench(fn,warmup=3,rep=12),idx))\n  except Exception: pass\n finalists=sorted(vals)[:35]; final=[]\n for _,idx in finalists:\n  fn=lambda idx=idx:torch.ops.aiter.hipb_mm(A,BT,idx)\n  final.append((triton.testing.do_bench(fn,warmup=8,rep=35),idx))\n tt=triton.testing.do_bench(lambda:torch.mm(A,BT),warmup=8,rep=35)\n best=sorted(final)[:12]; tops[m]=best\n y=torch.ops.aiter.hipb_mm(A,BT,best[0][1]);ref=torch.mm(A,BT)\n ratio=torch.isclose(y,ref,atol=.0365,rtol=.0009765625).float().mean().item();mx=(y-ref).abs().max().item()\n print('M',m,'torch',round(tt,5),'best',best,'ratio',ratio,'max',mx,'elapsed',round(time.time()-t0,1),flush=True)\naiter.hipb_destroy_extension();print('TOPS',tops)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
